    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by giving notice to the registrar"

-- src:1071 | (1A) The notice must include a statement that the new address is an appropriate address within the meaning given by section 86(2).
@ref s 87(1A) The notice must include a statement that the new address is an appropriate address (src:1071-1071)
GIVEN `a notice of a change of the address of the registered office is given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87(1A) the notice must include a statement that the new address is an appropriate address within the meaning given by section 86(2)` MEANS
    IF `a notice of a change of the address of the registered office is given`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The notice must include a statement"; there is no notice

-- src:1072 | (2) The change takes effect upon the notice being registered by the registrar, but until the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which it is registered a person may validly serve any document on the company at the address previously registered.
@ref s 87(2) The change takes effect upon the notice being registered (src:1072-1072)
GIVEN `the date on which the notice is registered by the registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87(2) the change takes effect on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the notice is registered by the registrar`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The change takes effect upon the notice being registered by the registrar" (the notice has not been registered)
    WHEN JUST registered THEN
        IF day AT LEAST registered
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The change takes effect upon the notice being registered by the registrar"

-- src:1072 | (2) The change takes effect upon the notice being registered by the registrar, but until the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which it is registered a person may validly serve any document on the company at the address previously registered.
@ref s 87(2) A person may validly serve a document at the address previously registered for 14 days (src:1072-1072)
GIVEN `the date on which the notice is registered by the registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87(2) a person may validly serve a document on the company at the address previously registered on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the notice is registered by the registrar`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period begins with the date on which the notice is registered
    WHEN JUST registered THEN
        BRANCH
            IF day BELOW registered THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period begins with the date on which the notice is registered
            IF day AT MOST (registered PLUS 13) THEN JUST TRUE -- the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which it is registered
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which it is registered"

-- src:1073 | (3) For the purposes of any duty of a company—
-- src:1074 | (a) to keep available for inspection at its registered office any register, index or other document, or
-- src:1075 | (b) to mention the address of its registered office in any document,
-- src:1076 | a company that has given notice to the registrar of a change in the address of its registered office may act on the change as from such date, not more than 14 days after the notice is given, as it may determine.
@ref s 87(3) The company may act on the change from a date not more than 14 days after the notice (src:1073-1076)
GIVEN `the date on which the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the date from which the company determines to act on the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87(3) the company may act on the change as from that date` MEANS
    IF `the date from which the company determines to act on the change` AT MOST (`the date on which the notice is given` PLUS 14)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may act on the change as from such date, not more than 14 days after the notice is given, as it may determine"

-- src:1077 | (4) Where a company unavoidably ceases to perform at its registered office any such duty as is mentioned in subsection (3)(a) in circumstances in which it was not practicable to give prior notice to the registrar of a change in the address of its registered office, but—
-- src:1078 | (a) resumes performance of that duty at other premises as soon as practicable, and
-- src:1079 | (b) gives notice accordingly to the registrar of a change in the situation of its registered office within 14 days of doing so,
-- src:1080 | it is not to be treated as having failed to comply with that duty.
@ref s 87(4) A duty unavoidably not performed at the old address: no failure (src:1077-1080)
GIVEN `the company unavoidably ceases to perform at its registered office a duty mentioned in subsection (3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was not practicable to give prior notice to the registrar of a change in the address of its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company resumes performance of that duty at other premises as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which it resumes performance` IS A DATE
      `the date on which it gives notice to the registrar of a change in the situation of its registered office` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87(4) the company is protected from being treated as having failed to comply with the duty` MEANS
    IF       `the company unavoidably ceases to perform at its registered office a duty mentioned in subsection (3)(a)`
         AND `it was not practicable to give prior notice to the registrar of a change in the address of its registered office`
         AND `the company resumes performance of that duty at other premises as soon as practicable`
         AND `the date on which it gives notice to the registrar of a change in the situation of its registered office` AT MOST (`the date on which it resumes performance` PLUS 14)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company unavoidably ceases to perform ... but— (a) resumes performance ..., and (b) gives notice ... within 14 days of doing so, it is not to be treated as having failed to comply with that duty"

